.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH ARACNE 1 2000-1月 "read_tf" "read_tf"
.SH NAME
read_tf \- Load the transcription factor gene symbols from a TF annotation table
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIread_tf(\fBfile\fR as string, 
\fBcolumn\fR as string = "Symbol", 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Load the transcription factor gene symbols from a TF annotation table
 (for example the \fBHomo_sapiens_TF.txt\fR of the AnimalTFDB style).
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfile\fB \fR\- 
 the file path of the TF annotation table: a tab/csv separated table whose header
 contains the **column** name, or a plain text file with one gene
 symbol per line. The empty/\fBNA\fR symbols are skipped and the result is unique
 in case insensitive.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcolumn\fB \fR\- the column name of the gene symbol, default \fBSymbol\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a character vector of the TF symbols
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
let TF = ARACNE::read_tf("G:/vcc2026/data/Homo_sapiens_TF.txt");
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
ARACNE
.SH FILES
.PP
TRNtoolkit.dll
.PP
